          &lt;td&gt;Research Vessel Kronprins Haakon&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expedition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;KH7010 (i2B)&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;16 August – 19 September 2025&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Days at sea&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;35&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Route&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;Longyearbyen, Yermak Plateau, Kvitøya Trough, Gakkel Ridge, Lomonosov Ridge, North Pole, Morris Jesup Spur, Longyearbyen&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Institutions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td&gt;University of Tromsø, NORCE, Alfred Wegener Institute, University of Bergen&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;post&#34;&gt;Post&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Standing on the sea ice, with over 4000 meters of ocean beneath my feet, felt almost unreal. I even played a soccer match there. Running in a survival suit was exhausting, but unforgettable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This expedition is something I am still processing. It taught me a lot, not only in science but also about myself. I often think back to my little town in Veneto, where this journey began. From that starting point, with all my ambitions, doubts, fears, and failures, I step by step arrived here: at the North Pole, on a research vessel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The path has not been easy. I have struggled many times, but I never gave up. And I could not have made it without the support of my family, friends, and even people who crossed my path only briefly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reaching the North Pole is something I will remember forever, especially in moments of struggle as a reminder of where I come from and how far my persistence and the support I have received can take me.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And yes, as if to make the moment even more surreal, a polar bear showed up later that day while we were sailing to the next station.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PS: A special thank you to Team B for making every shift fun and full of laughter.&lt;/p&gt;


